## 1. Execution rules

- One slice in progress at a time per owner.
- Each slice produces a verifiable check.
- Blocked slices update [`EXTERNAL_DEPENDENCY_ENABLEMENT_SPEC.md`](EXTERNAL_DEPENDENCY_ENABLEMENT_SPEC.md).
- A slice closes only after this document is updated with state, check result, residual gaps.

## 2. Tracker states

| State | Meaning |
| :--- | :--- |
| `planned` | Not started |
| `ready-backend` | Upstream contract available (or explicitly stubbed) |
| `in-progress` | Implementation under way |
| `blocked` | Halted by missing contract / pending decision |
| `qa-ready` | Implementation done; check pending |
| `done` | Check passed; docs updated |

## 3. Slice closure criteria

A slice is `done` only if:

1. The backend contract used is real or officially approved.
2. The integrated UI/client is reachable end-to-end.
3. There is at least one check specific to the slice.
4. Any residual gap is recorded in the tracker.

